      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per chat, I think we still need the SkShaper changes in order to pass the full language run context to SkUnicode\u0027s line break iterator (as there can be multiple languages tracked in SkShaper).  Maybe we can simplify the API in the future to take a single language per shape call, then we might be able to hide everything in SkUnicode.\n\nAnother potential issue with the SkUnicode approach is that now line breaking advances independent of segments: previously break iterators were scoped to the segment span, so SkShaper was fully consuming the break iterator for each segment.  Now that there can be segments with no break opportunities, we need some way to rewind the current break iter so it can be used for the next segment if in the same language run.  The buffering logic handles all that, and if we were to do it in skunicode we\u0027d need a way to cheaply rewind or recreate the iterator.  I guess we could use the same buffering approach, but it would probably need some API changes (rewind).",
